          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "name",
            "text": "atlas-sdk 1.8.0",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "desc",
            "text": "Official JavaScript client for the Atlas deterministic simulation runtime: start a world, step it, read a machine, replay a run."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "install",
            "text": "npm i atlas-sdk",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
              "size": 13,
              "padding": 8,
              "background": "#f4f4f4",
              "radius": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "meta",
            "text": "Version 1.8.0 · License Apache-2.0 · 156,000 weekly downloads · Maintainer northstar · Published 2026"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "readme-h",
            "text": "README",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "atlas-sdk wraps the Atlas HTTP and WebSocket protocol in typed calls. Create a world from a seed, advance it by ticks, inspect any machine and diff two runs. Every call is deterministic given the world seed and the order of calls, which the SDK enforces by serialising them. Requires an Atlas server; the package includes an in-process stub for tests."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "example",
            "text": "import {Atlas} from 'atlas-sdk';\nconst world = await Atlas.connect('http://localhost:7000').world({seed: 42});\nawait world.step(100);\nconsole.log(await world.machine('alice-mac').screen());",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
              "size": 13,
              "padding": 8,
              "background": "#f4f4f4",
              "radius": 4
            }
          },
