            "text": "A clock that only moves when you tell it to. Drop-in for Date.now and setTimeout in tests and simulations."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "install",
            "text": "npm i deterministic-clock",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
              "size": 13,
              "padding": 8,
              "background": "#f4f4f4",
              "radius": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "meta",
            "text": "Version 0.9.3 · License MIT · 240,000 weekly downloads · Maintainer northstar · Published 2026"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "readme-h",
            "text": "README",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "deterministic-clock replaces the wall clock with a logical one. now() returns the current tick, advance(ms) moves it and fires any timers due, and install() patches the globals for the duration of a test. Timers fire in order of due time, then registration order, so a run is the same every time."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "example",
            "text": "import {clock} from 'deterministic-clock';\nclock.install();\nsetTimeout(() => console.log('fired'), 1000);\nclock.advance(1000); // prints 'fired'",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
              "size": 13,
              "padding": 8,
              "background": "#f4f4f4",
              "radius": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "deps-h",
            "text": "Dependencies (0)",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "deps-none",
            "text": "None."
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "id": "repo",
            "text": "Repository on GitHub",
            "url": "http://github.com/"
          }
        ]
