          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "readme-h",
            "text": "README",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "zod-lite covers objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, literals, unions, optional and nullable, with parse() and safeParse(). Errors are a flat list of path and message. It does not do transforms, refinements or async; use the full library if you need them. json-diff-lite is used to report what safeParse would have to change."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "example",
            "text": "import {z} from 'zod-lite';\nconst User = z.object({id: z.number(), name: z.string()});\ntype User = z.infer<typeof User>;\nUser.parse({id: 1, name: 'alice'});",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
